    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `initials` field is exposed on the `GET /api/owners/{id}` response, which serializes an `OwnerDto` produced by `OwnerMapper`. Two edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the existing `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` has the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` that computes it:\n   ```java\n   Character.toUpperCase(firstName.charAt(0)) + \".\" + Character.toUpperCase(lastName.charAt(0)) + \".\"\n   ```\n   For `firstName=\"john\"`, `lastName=\"smith\"` this yields `\"J.S.\"`, matching the spec and the `coreComputesInitials` acceptance test.\n\nThis follows the codebase's existing pattern (the same expression-based approach used for `displayName`) rather than introducing a new OfficeFloor function, since the derivation is a pure DTO mapping concern.",
